From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toluwaleke Ogundipe <anonymoux47@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:33:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] Recover from GPU resets

Create the GL context with reset notification and, when the driver reports
that the context was lost, recreate the EGL and Cogl contexts and restore
every GPU resource the compositor owns: stage views, onscreens, window
textures (SHM buffers are held until the next commit so they can be
uploaded again), backgrounds, cursors, text, actor effects and screencast
streams. Frame dispatch pauses while the reset is in progress, and the
compositor exits gracefully if restoring fails.

The compositor enables this through
meta_context_enable_cogl_display_features() with
COGL_DISPLAY_FEATURE_RESET_NOTIFICATION. Shell resources listen to the
ClutterGraphicsRecoveryContext signals to recreate their own textures.

This is GNOME/mutter!5247 by Toluwaleke Ogundipe, squashed onto Mutter 51
with the window corner API kept next to the new shaped texture realize
and unrealize functions.
